{"name":"Tall Ships","hex":"#0e81b9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tall ships","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of tall ship"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tall_ships"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tall Ships (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Tall Ships were an English indie rock band, formed in 2009 whilst studying in Falmouth and based in Brighton, England. The band was composed of lead singer/guitarist Ric Phethean, bassist/backing vocalist Matt Parker, drummer Jamie Bush and keyboardist James Elliot Field."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Tall_ships_at_common_people.JPG/330px-Tall_ships_at_common_people.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tall_Ships_(band)"},{"title":"Tall Ships (video installation)","blocks":[{"text":"Tall Ships (1992) is a multi-channel, silent video installation created by American new-media artist Gary Hill. The work was commissioned by curator Jan Hoet for Documenta 9 (1992), an edition of the international art exhibition held every five years in Kassel, Germany. It was selected for the Whitney Biennial in 1993 and has been exhibited at museums around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f6/Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tall_Ships_(video_installation)"},{"title":"Tall ship","blocks":[{"text":"A tall ship is a large, traditionally rigged sailing vessel. Popular modern tall ship rigs include topsail schooners, brigantines, brigs and barques. \"Tall ship\" can also be defined more specifically by an organization, such as for a race or festival."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Tall_ship_off_of_Newlyn_3.jpg/330px-Tall_ship_off_of_Newlyn_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tall_ship"},{"title":"Ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ship is a large watercraft designed for travel across the surface of a body of water, carrying cargo or passengers, or in support of specialized tasks such as warfare, oceanography and fishing. Ships are generally distinguished from boats, based on size, shape, load capacity and purpose. Ships have supported exploration, trade, warfare, migration, colonization, and science. Ship transport is responsible for the largest portion of world commerce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg/330px-Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ship"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f6/Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f6/Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Gary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gary Hill, Tall Ships, multi-channel video installation, 90' x 10' x 10', installation view, 1992.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGary_Hill_Tall_Ships_Installation_view.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Gary_Hill_TallShips_Detail.tif/lossy-page1-250px-Gary_Hill_TallShips_Detail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/65/Gary_Hill_TallShips_Detail.tif/lossy-page1-250px-Gary_Hill_TallShips_Detail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gary Hill, Tall Ships, multi-channel video installation, 90' x 10' x 10', detail, 1992.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGary_Hill_TallShips_Detail.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg/500px-Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg/1280px-Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg/500px-Hanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Group of \"tall ships\" at Hanse Sail 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHanse_sail_2010_warnemuende_einlaufen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg/500px-Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg/1280px-Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg/500px-Kruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The tall ship Kruzenshtern","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKruzenshterns_f%C3%B6r.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Portsmouthsunset.jpg/330px-Portsmouthsunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimed